 the game puts you in these really  intense situations and you feel like  you're just a hundred percent hopeless  and helpless and most the time I felt  like that was a good thing because  everything is dynamic it felt like maybe  I just had bad luck that time I should  have jumped a little higher and you  wouldn't have caught me and smashed me  onto the ground or I could have it could  have thrown the brick a different way  which would have helped me out later on  in the level so you learn little things  but even if your play is perfect they're  just times when you know it sucks and  you die and that's the way it is it was  a good feeling to me that it's not  always just my fault sometimes the world  just says you're you're gonna die in  this scenario you're caught and and  you're done for it made me feel like the  world was against me and it was up to me  to play well and also utilize everything  that I could to survive some of the  enemies like this weird Hedgehog monster  and they change based on what you do so  if I jump a little higher he might turn  around and grab me right out of the air  but if I run away he will chase me and  these guys are actually faster than you  so you can't just run away from them  they will catch you and typically they  end up picking me up and throwing me  against these rocks and you just feel  super helpless so you eventually have to  turn around and hit them with something  and it won't even actually stop them  most of the time they just like batted  away and keep trying to destroy you but  if you keep at it you know you really  can feel like you can actually  accomplish something and this tiny  little guy that you are I can actually  do something in the world it's brutal  and it's heartbreaking but it's  incredibly engrossing and the game is a  little short I burned through it in like  an hour so it's not very long and  because it's got puzzles in it I don't  know about the replay value because you  know some people might enjoy replaying  it and trying to beat it quicker or  something but that's not really my style  I probably won't you replay it  and I was hoping the environments would  change more as well I always felt like I  was in the same area you're typically  either in the forest or this underground  cavern area but they look very similar  so I never really felt a huge amount of  progression overall though I felt like  the art and the music and the gameplay  did a really good job of putting me in  this frightening world and making me  root for this little fuzzball creature  and and I just really wanted to survive  and that pretty much sums up most of my  thoughts you can get it on steam for  fifteen dollars but I bet it'll go on  sale at some point if that feels a  little high I hope you guys liked this  style of video and let me know your  thoughts thanks for watching bye
 

